# SPY0132: '_' placeholder used outside a function call / operator context.
# When '_' is not defined as a variable and appears as a bare expression, the
# specific diagnostic fires instead of the generic UndefinedVariable.
#
# History: this fixture used `print(_)`, which is a placeholder INSIDE a call —
# a partial application, never SPY0132 — and its sidecar matched the word
# "placeholder" in the SPY0908 text's file path (vacuous). `print(_)` as a
# statement is the SPY0603 cell in statements/expression_statement_refuse_placeholder_1622.

def main():
    x = _
    print(x)
